{
  "moduleId": "m00203",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00203:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Alcohols from Carbonyl Compounds: Reduction"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "ad84026c-2f49-42c8-af88-badad9e60846"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "A carbonyl compound undergoes reduction to form an alcohol, where a bond to hydrogen is added to the carbonyl carbon."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00203:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Reduction of Aldehydes and Ketones"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00002",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00002"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00002",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00002-alt",
              "text": "An aldehyde undergoes reduction to form a primary alcohol, a ketone undergoes reduction to form a secondary alcohol. In both cases, a bond to hydrogen is added to carbonyl carbon."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_002.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00003",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00003"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00003",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00003-alt",
              "text": "Two reductions. Butanal reacts first with sodium borohydride and ethanol, then hydronium to form 1-butanol. Dicyclohexyl ketone reacts first with sodium borohydride and ethanol, then hydronium to form dicyclohexylmethanol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_003.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00004",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00004"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00004",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00004-alt",
              "text": "2-cyclohexenone reacts first with lithium aluminum hydride and ether, then hydronium ion to form 2-cyclohexenol with 94 percent yield."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00005",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00005"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00005",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00005-alt",
              "text": "A carbonyl compound reacts with hydrogen anion having an electron pair to form an alkoxide ion intermediate. This reacts with hydronium ion to form an alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00006",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00006"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00006",
          "class": "scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00203:caption:fig-00006-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00006-alt",
              "text": "Acetoacetyl A C P reacts with nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydrogen to form beta-hydroxybutyryl A C P and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide plus cation."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_006.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00002",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00203:title:sect-00002-title",
        "text": "Reduction of Carboxylic Acids and Esters"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00007",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00007"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00007",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00007-alt",
              "text": "A carboxylic acid or an ester undergoes reduction to form a primary alcohol. In each case, the carbonyl oxygen becomes a hydroxy, and the carbon gains two hydrogens."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_007.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00008",
          "segmentId": "m00203:para:para-00008"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00008",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00203:alt:fig-00008-alt",
              "text": "9-octadecenoic acid reacts first with lithium aluminum hydride and ether, then hydronium to form 9-octadecen-1-ol. Methyl-2-pentenoate reacts first with lithium aluminum hydride and ether, then hydronium, forming 2-penten-1-ol and methanol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_04_008.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "id": "exam-00001",
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00203:example-title:exam-00001-title",
            "text": "Identifying a Reactant, Given the Product"
          },
          "content": [
